    :ordinary-admission
    :as-of-admission
    :filtered-since-history-refusal
    :as-of-over-speculative-refusal]}
  :witnesses
  {:datomic
   {:mechanism :committed-log-transaction-instant
    :notes "d/basis-t reports the underlying basis through an as-of window; re-applying d/as-of at that basis replaces the window, so the value's latest claimed transaction is compared against the committed head's :db/txInstant."}
   :datahike
   {:mechanism :committed-max-tx-transaction-instant
    :notes "AsOfDB is witnessed through the :origin-db it carries whole; the origin's :max-tx transaction instant must match the committed head."}
   :datascript
   {:mechanism :connection-committed-value-registry
    :notes "No transaction metadata exists, so committedness is decided by identity against the connection's current value or its listener-recorded committed states (bounded, newest-first by :max-tx)."
    :additional-refusal-suite eacl.datascript.snapshot-lifecycle-test}
   :datalevin
   {:mechanism :read-snapshot-gate
    :notes "A Datalevin read snapshot is an open LMDB read transaction over committed store state; no speculative-transaction value satisfies read-snapshot?, so the value itself is the witness. The pre-existing basis-kind gate already refused every other shape."}}}
